  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2005-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "As a product of primes, \\(3! \\cdot 5! \\cdot 7! = 2^8 \\cdot 3^4 \\cdot 5^2 \\cdot 7.\\) A cube divisor uses exponents that are multiples of \\(3:\\) the exponent of \\(2\\) can be \\(0,\\) \\(3,\\) or \\(6\\) (\\(3\\) choices), the exponent of \\(3\\) can be \\(0\\) or \\(3\\) (\\(2\\) choices), and the exponents of \\(5\\) and \\(7\\) must be \\(0.\\) That gives \\(3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 = 6\\) cubes.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(3! \\cdot 5! \\cdot 7!\\) as a product of prime powers",
        "A cube divisor uses each prime to an exponent that is a multiple of \\(3;\\) count the allowed exponents for each prime"
      ],
